<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36395" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pīpŭlum</span></b> , i,
			n., and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pīpŭlus</span></b> , i, m.
		pipo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a peeping</i>, <i>piping</i>, <i>chirping;</i> hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A whimpering</i>, <i>crying</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">filioli,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Front. Ep. ad Anton. 1, 3</span></i>
			 Mai.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>An outcry</i>, <i>upbraiding</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">te pipulo hic differam ante aedes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Aul. 3, 2, 32</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pipulo te differam id est convicio, declinatum
					a pipatu pullorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 7, § 103</span></i>
			 Müll.: pipulo poscere, Cn. Matius ap. <i><span class="en">Gell. 20,
				9, 4</span></i>.</div>
